hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2844","Narrated Abu Hurairah:The Prophet (ﷺ) as saying: If anyone gets a dog"
"2845","Narrated Abdullah ibn Mughaffal: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: Were dogs not a species of creature I should command that they all be killed; but kill every pure black one"
"2846","Narrated Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) ordered to kill dogs"
"2847","Narrated 'Abi b. Hatim:I asked the Prophet (ﷺ) "
"2848","Narrated 'Adi b. Hatim:I asked the Messenger of Allah. I said: We hunt with these dogs. He replied: When you set off your dog and mention Allah's name over it"
"2849","Narrated 'Adi b. Hatim:The Prophet (ﷺ) as saying: When you shoot your arrow and mention Allah's name"
"2850","Narrated 'Adi b. Hatim:The Prophet (ﷺ) as saying: When the animal at which you shot falls in water"
"2851","Narrated Adi ibn Hatim: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: Eat what ever is caught for you by a dog or a hawk you have trained and set off when you have mentioned Allah's name. I said: (Does this apply) if it killed (the animal)? He said: When it kills it without eating any of it"
"2852","Narrated AbuTha'labah al-Khushani: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said about the game hunted by a dog: If you set off your dog and have mentioned Allah's name"
"2853","Narrated Adi ibn Hatim: Messenger of Allah"
"2854","Narrated 'Adi b. Hatim:I asked Prophet (ﷺ) about featherless arrow. He said: If it strikes with its end"
"2855","Narrated Abu Taa'labat b. al-Khushani:I said: Messenger of Allah"
"2856","Narrated AbuTha'labah al-Khushani: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: AbuTha'labah"
"2857","Narrated Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-'As: There was a bedouin called AbuTha'labah. He said: Messenger of Allah"
"2858","Narrated AbuWaqid: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: Whatever is cut off of an animal when it is alive is dead"
"2859","Narrated Abdullah ibn Abbas: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: (the narrator Sufyan said: I do not know but that it [the tradition] has been transmitted from the Prophet (ﷺ): He who lives in the desert will become rude; he who pursues the game will be negligent"
"2860","Narrated AbuHurayrah: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: He said: He who sticks to a king is perverted. This version adds: The nearer a servant (of Allah) goes to a king"
"2861","Narrated AbuTha'labah al-Khushani: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: When you shoot your arrow (and the animal goes out of your sight) and you come three days later on it"
"2862","Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Umar:The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying: It is the duty of a Muslim man who has something which is to be given as bequest not to have it for two nights without having his will written regarding it"